						<ProtectedString name="Source">--Hello, it&apos;s the creator of the talking brick. I will give you instructions on how to use this correctly. Let&apos;s begin with step 1.
--1. Rename the model - If you want a long talk, don&apos;t double-click the model and rename it. Click the model once, on properties, change &quot;Model&quot; on name and click enter! Here are the things
--YOU MUST NOT DO.

--1. Ungroup it - If you ungroup it, it will let you change the name for the workspace. That&apos;s not a great idea, eh? So leave it as model.
--2. Delete the humanoid - The humanoid detects the brick and puts the model name above the brick. If you delete it, it will not be able to talk at all.
--3. Change the brick&apos;s name - The humanoid puts the model&apos;s name only on top of the brick which name is Head. Nobody can change that. So don&apos;t change it to anything else except Head.
--4. Change the transparency to 1 - If you change it to 1, the text just stops working. Try &quot;0.9&quot;.

--Here are things you should do:

--Put in anti-lag scripts - People have proven that those just make lag, but I have proven that it&apos;s real. I deleted all my antilag scripts and it was unbearably laggy.
--Make a tycoon with this brick - You may think I&apos;m desprate and crazy, but there are always text on top of those buy bricks that tell you what you&apos;re buying and how much it is. This model
--can easily help you with making a tycoon.
--Put these on top of obby givers - This tells the user what is &quot;in the brick&quot;. So if you have RainbowPath, you should rename the model &quot;RainbowPath&quot; and put it on top of the giver.

--The text under makes everything work. Don&apos;t change it.

